{"id":"2610.31372","authors":[{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc6834577d","user":{"_id":"68f5cfb57b23d048745eb8a9","avatarUrl":"/avatars/8fc6894470f36700410a38b7faef7805.svg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Jiening Siow","user":"Little-d1d1","type":"user","name":"Little-d1d1"},"name":"Jiening Siow","status":"claimed_verified","statusLastChangedAt":"2026-10-23T16:45:04.648Z","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc6834577e","user":{"_id":"660bf98c3336a7e128a0e918","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/660bf98c3336a7e128a0e918/lpketCvJ3Kgx5ucN0-HWo.jpeg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Amy Xin","user":"amyxx2001","type":"user","name":"amyxx2001"},"name":"Amy Xin","status":"claimed_verified","statusLastChangedAt":"2026-10-23T16:45:04.637Z","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc6834577f","name":"Junjie Wang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc68345780","name":"Ziyu Tang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc68345781","name":"Zijun Yao","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc68345782","name":"Yunjia Qi","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc68345783","name":"Fanjin Zhang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc68345784","name":"Lei Hou","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc68345785","name":"Jie Tang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adb551b121a70fc68345786","name":"Juanzi Li","hidden":false}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z","submittedOnDailyAt":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z","title":"RIDAR: Safeguarding Research Integrity in Autonomous Research Agents via Automated Detection and Runtime Intervention","submittedOnDailyBy":{"_id":"68f5cfb57b23d048745eb8a9","avatarUrl":"/avatars/8fc6894470f36700410a38b7faef7805.svg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Jiening Siow","user":"Little-d1d1","type":"user","name":"Little-d1d1"},"summary":"Autonomous research agents are increasingly used to automate large portions of scientific research, yet they are prone to research integrity violations (RIVs): behaviors that compromise the validity, reproducibility, or faithfulness of the research process. We present RIDAR, a framework for automated RIV detection and runtime intervention. First, we introduce RIVT, a comprehensive taxonomy of 14 RIV types spanning the full research lifecycle. Building on RIVT, we present RIDAR-post-hoc, a framework to detect RIVs within agent trajectories. RIDAR-post-hoc achieves 85.2% F1 performance on RIV-Gold, a benchmark for RIV detection with 60 expert-annotated trajectories. Applying RIDAR-post-hoc to RIV-Wild, a dataset of 300 agent trajectories across 50 distinct research tasks, we detect 3,964 RIV instances in 99.7% of trajectories, revealing the prevalence of RIVs in current agents. Finally, we present RIDAR-runtime, a framework for dynamically detecting and correcting RIVs during agent runtime. RIDAR-runtime effectively reduces agent RIVs remaining at task completion by 36.8%. We will release our code and data to facilitate future research.","upvotes":7,"discussionId":"6adb551c121a70fc68345787","githubRepo":"https://github.com/THU-KEG/RIDAR","githubRepoAddedBy":"user","ai_summary":"RIDAR detects and mitigates research integrity violations in autonomous agents via taxonomy-based post-hoc analysis and real-time intervention.","ai_keywords":["research integrity violations","RIVT","RIDAR-post-hoc","RIDAR-runtime","agent trajectories","F1 performance","runtime intervention"],"ai_summary_model":"thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small","githubStars":4,"organization":{"_id":"64db4fc57266618e854318f4","name":"THU-KEG","fullname":"Knowledge Engineer Group @ Tsinghua University","avatar":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/648c4b46e549be47af1aafcd/5atqdE9AUWvYAHm9FNkG_.png"},"linkedModels":[],"numTotalModels":0,"linkedDatasets":[{"author":"THU-KEG","downloads":24,"gated":false,"id":"THU-KEG/RIDAR","lastModified":"2026-10-23T12:36:45.000Z","private":false,"repoType":"dataset","likes":0,"isLikedByUser":false,"isBenchmark":false,"isTraces":false,"isEnvironment":false}],"numTotalDatasets":1,"linkedSp